# THE finding from the first batch: the robot does not go blind, it PARKS.
#
#   nav2: "Reached the goal! / Goal succeeded"  ... then nothing, ever again
#
# Once it stops, the carrot stops moving with it, --min-goal-shift suppresses
# the next publish, and with no new goal there is no reason to move. The
# stillness sustains itself. Every run in the first batch spent 59-96% of its
# time in a single stall that never ended.
#
# Two changes under test here:
#   * re-send the goal after 6 s without moving, breaking the deadlock
#   * always log a change of state, and repeat it every 10 s while it holds,
#     so a stopped robot can never again be silent in the log
set -uo pipefail
cd "$ESDA_HOME"
./demo.sh lap igvc_wavy_test --seconds 420 \
  --note "goal heartbeat + visible idle logging" \
  -- --lane-memory 3.0 --lidar-corridor
